# Density estimates: geom_density

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`geom_density()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/geom_density.html), which covers
`stat_density()` too, in the order the page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and
then Giggly's. An example Giggly cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is
waiting for, so the page is also a list of what remains.

`geom_density()` draws a kernel density estimate, a smoothed version of the histogram, which suits
continuous data drawn from a smooth distribution; `stat_density()` computes it. Besides the
density, the stat computes counts, the density times the number of rows, for stacking densities.
Giggly has none of this yet. Every example uses ggplot2's `diamonds`, which is not in Giggly yet
either.

## A density curve

```r
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat)) +
  geom_density()
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and `stat_density()`.

## Horizontal densities

```r
# Map the values to y to flip the orientation
ggplot(diamonds, aes(y = carat)) +
  geom_density()
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and `stat_density()`.

## Rougher and smoother curves

```r
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat)) +
  geom_density(adjust = 1/5)
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat)) +
  geom_density(adjust = 5)
```

`adjust` multiplies the bandwidth the density is smoothed over. Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()`
and its `adjust` option.

## A curve for each cut

```r
ggplot(diamonds, aes(depth, colour = cut)) +
  geom_density() +
  xlim(55, 70)
ggplot(diamonds, aes(depth, fill = cut, colour = cut)) +
  geom_density(alpha = 0.1) +
  xlim(55, 70)
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and `stat_density()`.

## Bounded data

```r
# Use `bounds` to adjust computation for known data limits
big_diamonds <- diamonds[diamonds$carat >= 1, ]
ggplot(big_diamonds, aes(carat)) +
  geom_density(color = 'red') +
  geom_density(bounds = c(1, Inf), color = 'blue')
```

The diamonds of a carat or more have no values below 1, which the red curve, knowing no bounds,
smooths past. Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and its `bounds` option.

## Stacked densities

```r
# Stacked density plots: if you want to create a stacked density plot, you
# probably want to 'count' (density * n) variable instead of the default
# density
# Loses marginal densities
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat, fill = cut)) +
  geom_density(position = "stack")
# Preserves marginal densities
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat, after_stat(count), fill = cut)) +
  geom_density(position = "stack")
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and `stat_density()`.

## Conditional densities

```r
# You can use position="fill" to produce a conditional density estimate
ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat, after_stat(count), fill = cut)) +
  geom_density(position = "fill")
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_density()` and `stat_density()`, and `position_fill()`.